# Version shipping

This is the one rule for how work ships in this repository. `AGENTS.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, the `complete-next-version` and `release-version` skills and the `/complete-next-version` command point here.

## The version

- A milestone's version is the `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` at the start of its GitHub milestone title, with an optional suffix: `v1.3.0 Beta: Public UX & compliance`. Read it from the title, never from GitHub's milestone number.
- **The next version** is the open milestone with the lowest version above the latest released tag, compared as semver (`v1.9.0` < `v1.10.0`). `composer milestone:next` prints it with its branch, PR and release titles.
- Semantic versioning: MAJOR for breaking changes, MINOR for features, PATCH for fixes. The milestone title sets the version, so issues never bump it.
- Stop and report to Bambie, without guessing, if a milestone title does not start with a valid `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, or its version is not above the latest tag, or the version is already taken on `main`. Don't rename, create or delete milestones yourself.

## Names built from the version

| Item | Format | Example (`v1.3.0 Beta: Public UX & compliance`) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Milestone branch | `milestone/v<MAJOR>-<MINOR>-<PATCH>-<slug>` | `milestone/v1-3-0-public-ux-compliance` |
| Milestone PR into `main` | `v<version>: <milestone name>` | `v1.3.0: Public UX & compliance` |
| Issue PR into the milestone branch | `[v<version>] <issue title> (#<issue>)` | `[v1.3.0] Branded error pages (#123)` |
| Commits | Conventional Commits with `Refs #<issue>` | `fix: keep the tag filter on reload (Refs #123)` |
| Release note | `changelog/releases/v<version>.json` (see `docs/change-log-hub.md`) | `changelog/releases/v1.3.0.json` |
| Tag | `v<version>` | `v1.3.0` |
| GitHub Release title | `v<version> <milestone name>` | `v1.3.0 Public UX & compliance` |

- Never write "Milestone 7", "#7", "[#7]", "M7" or "/milestone/7" in a branch, title, commit subject, tag or release.
- Check names with `composer milestone:check-title -- "<title>"`, `composer milestone:check-branch -- "<branch>"` and `composer milestone:check-release -- vX.Y.Z "<release title>"`. CI runs the title and branch checks on every pull request.
- Version fields: this repository has none. The tag is the version. `composer milestone:bump -- vX.Y.Z` creates the release note from its template if no PR has yet.

## The flow: one version ships once

1. **Start.** Run the live preview gate (`laragon-local-dev.mdc`). Then `composer milestone:next`. Create the milestone branch from `origin/main` if it is missing (`git push -u origin HEAD`), otherwise merge `origin/main` into it. Merge `origin/dependencies` into it with a merge commit. Stop on any conflict.
2. **Work.** Commit every issue in the milestone on the milestone branch, or on a short `<type>/<issue>-<slug>` branch merged into it by an issue PR. Small Conventional Commits with `Refs #<n>`. Open one draft PR into `main` titled `v<version>: <milestone name>`, listing `Closes #<n>` for every issue. Post the Committed comment on each issue when its work is committed (`Add-IssueUpdate.ps1`); it closes when the milestone PR merges.
3. **Merge.** Run `composer milestone:bump -- vX.Y.Z`, finish `changelog/releases/vX.Y.Z.json` by `docs/change-log-hub.md`, and make that the last commit, `chore: release vX.Y.Z`. `gh pr ready`, wait for CI to go green, then ask the ship-gate question (`ship-gate` skill). On "merge": `gh pr merge --merge`, one merge commit, never a squash or rebase.
4. **Release.** Push one tag `vX.Y.Z` on that merge commit. `release.yml` checks the tag is on `main` and publishes the GitHub Release titled `v<version> <milestone name>`.
5. **Deploy.** One Cloudron deploy of that tag: `gh workflow run deploy.yml -f tag=vX.Y.Z`. It refuses a tag that is not on `main` or has no published Release, takes a backup, uploads one archive, migrates, activates, restarts, checks `/health` and rolls back on failure. Evidence is the green run on that tag.
6. **Close out** with `Close-IssueTree.ps1` and `Close-Milestone.ps1`, then merge `origin/main` into `dependencies`.

## Hotfixes

Only with Bambie's approval through AskQuestion, recorded on the issue: a `cursor/fix/<issue>-<slug>` branch from `origin/main`, released as `vX.Y.(Z+1)` through the same merge, release and deploy steps, then `main` merged back into the open milestone branch.

## Never

- Force-push, `reset --hard` or rebase a shared branch.
- Merge, tag, release or deploy after a single issue, or without the ship-gate answer in the current chat.
- Deploy a branch, or claim a step happened without its command output.
